Notes: The available GX discovery result exposes one logical device on can0 with connection-id/node 0x0. The current tool accepts only node 0x0 and identifies one CAN bus as one logical BSLBATT device; it cannot enumerate or select individual battery modules. The BSL 16-series (16串) description refers to the battery cell-series configuration and does not prove that multiple BMS modules are connected. No verified hardware setup with at least two independently identifiable modules was available, and the BMS protocol behavior for a multi-module system has not been confirmed: it is unknown whether only the master is updated, the master broadcasts firmware to slaves, or every module requires a separate update. Executing one ordinary node-0 upgrade would therefore not provide valid evidence that all modules were updated. This case must remain blocked until the battery/BMS team defines the multi-module mechanism and supplies a test setup with at least two modules whose versions can be independently checked before and after the update.
